* Bench functional model. Two source-to-source devices block the terminal
* voltage in either direction when the independent gate permit is low.
* The symmetric clamp carries feeder inductive current during turn-off.
.subckt BENCH_DC_CUT A B ENABLE params: RON=4.4m ROFF=100meg FALL=100n
Rgate ENABLE g 1k
Cgate g 0 {FALL/(1k*0.69314718)}
Bqa A mid I={v(A,mid)*(1/ROFF+0.5*(1+tanh((v(g)-1.65)/0.15))/RON)}
Bqb B mid I={v(B,mid)*(1/ROFF+0.5*(1+tanh((v(g)-1.65)/0.15))/RON)}
Dqa mid A BODY
Dqb mid B BODY
.model BODY D(IS=50n N=1.3 RS=5m CJO=1n)
* Bidirectional piecewise-linear fixture clamp. The model omits package
* inductance and limits the slope beyond the assumed 33 V knee.
Bclamp A B I={(max(v(A,B)-33,0)+min(v(A,B)+33,0))/0.23}
.ends BENCH_DC_CUT

* A separate current-window and latch can open the DC path even when both
* bridge gates remain requested or the bridge devices have failed closed.
.subckt BENCH_DC_CUT_CONTROL AMPS PG ARM RUN READY ENABLE params: DELAY=200n TRIP_AMPS=6
Vhealthy peer 0 3.3
Xlocal AMPS PG ARM RUN peer READY ENABLE BENCH_DC_CUT_LINKED DELAY={DELAY} TRIP_AMPS={TRIP_AMPS}
.ends BENCH_DC_CUT_CONTROL

* PEER is the default-low health signal received from the other rail.
.subckt BENCH_DC_CUT_LINKED AMPS PG ARM RUN PEER READY ENABLE params: DELAY=200n TRIP_AMPS=6
Btrip state 0 V={1.65*(1-tanh((abs(v(AMPS))-TRIP_AMPS)/0.15))}
Rtrip state ok 1k
Ctrip ok 0 {DELAY/(1k*0.69314718)}
Vhealthy upstream 0 3.3
Xlatch ok ok PG ARM RUN upstream PEER READY ENABLE BRIDGE_LOCAL_SHUTDOWN
.ends BENCH_DC_CUT_LINKED
